# Frontend Architecture

This is a React + TypeScript SPA (Vite) with MUI, TanStack Query, and Axios.

## Directory Structure

```
frontend/src/
  app/              # App-level wiring only (providers, router, auth context)
  config/           # Static config (theme.ts, queryClient.ts, constants.ts)
  lib/              # Framework-agnostic utilities (api/axios.ts, api/types.ts)
  hooks/            # Global shared hooks (useAuth, useNotification, useThemeMode, useSidebar)
  types/            # Global shared types (models.ts, api.ts, index.ts barrel)
  layouts/          # Layout shells (DashboardLayout, AuthLayout, layouts/components/)
  features/         # Feature modules -- one folder per domain
  components/       # Shared cross-feature UI components
```

## Import Rules

- Always use `@/` path alias (maps to `src/`). Never use relative `../../` chains.
- Barrel re-exports (`index.ts`) are only allowed in `types/`. Features must NOT have barrel files.
- Import order: react/react-dom -> third-party -> @/ aliases -> relative.

## Provider Hierarchy (do not reorder)

ThemeModeProvider > QueryClientProvider > BrowserRouter > AuthProvider > SidebarProvider > NotificationProvider

## State Management

- **Context API** for UI state: auth, theme mode, sidebar, notifications.
- **TanStack Query** for all server/async state. No manual `useEffect` + `useState` for data fetching.
- **No Redux** unless a genuinely cross-cutting complex client state emerges that Context cannot handle cleanly.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode. Zero `any`. No `@ts-ignore`.
- Shared domain models live in `types/models.ts`. API shapes in `types/api.ts`.
- Feature-scoped types live in `features/<name>/interfaces/<name>.interfaces.ts`.
- Component props interfaces are defined in the feature's `interfaces/` file, not inline.
